---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="Your private invitation">
<script is:inline slot="head">window.__inviteToken = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1)).get('token'); history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname);</script>
<main id="main" class="invite-page"><a href="/" class="brand"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">u<span>c</span></span><span>unreel content<span class="brand-sub">THE CLIENT SPACE</span></span></a><section class="invite-card panel"><span class="eyebrow">AN INVITATION TO YOUR WORKSPACE</span><h1>Let’s bring the<br/>picture into focus<span>.</span></h1><p>You’ve been invited to view results for the accounts or projects shared with your email address.</p><div class="scope-box"><strong>View. Understand. Stay in the loop.</strong><p>This is read-only access to your assigned targets. It does not allow editing metrics, publishing content, or viewing other clients’ work.</p></div><p id="invite-status" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking your invitation…</p><p>Use the Google or email sign-in options shown below, as available. No Clerk project or developer account is needed.</p><div id="invite-sign-in" class="clerk-container" hidden></div><div id="invite-preview" class="scope-box" hidden><h2 id="invite-target"></h2><p id="invite-scope"></p><p id="invite-expiry"></p></div><button id="accept-invite" class="primary" hidden>Accept read-only access <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button id="retry-invite" class="text-button" hidden>Try again</button><button id="switch-account" class="text-button" hidden>Sign out to use another account</button><p class="small">Sign in with the email address your invitation was sent to. If sign-in redirects or you reload this page, reopen the original invitation email link after signing in. Your invitation is never placed in a redirect URL or saved in browser storage.</p><p class="small">An expired or revoked invitation cannot be accepted. Ask your workspace administrator for a fresh invitation. Never forward your invitation.</p><a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to unreel content</a></section><p class="invite-footnote">A private space for the work you’re building.</p></main>
<script>import '../scripts/invite';</script>
</Shell>
